  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1240 PM CDT Sun Oct 4 2026\n\nDry NW H5 flow and sprawling surface high pressure will keep the\nweather quiet across the region for the next several days.\nTemperatures will remain near normal today through Tuesday.\nHowever, as H5 heights rise, temperatures will begin to slowly\nwarm up for the second half of the work week. By Friday, the\narea will see temperatures about 5-10 degrees above normal. \n\nThe only significant adjustment to the forecast from yesterday\nis the introduction of PoPs (25-40%) for areas south of the Ohio\nRiver Saturday night into Sunday. This is in response to better\nmodel agreement that tropical Gulf moisture will be drawn north\ninto the OH/TN valleys (possibly remnants of a tropical\ndisturbance?), and it is possible precipitation chances could\nlinger through the second half of next weekend. The details are\nvery muddy at this point, so expect additional changes to the\nforecast in the coming days for this time period.",
